IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation "version in force from 6/5/2026 to 20/10/2026":
-- PART 10A, TRANSFER OF REGISTRATION: s 364 (duties of the company with respect to the issue of certificates), lines 23546 to 23586 of CoA1967.txt.
-- s 364A (regulations) is machinery that hands the detail to the Minister's regulations under section 411; it is `inert` in NOTES.md, reason 2.
--
-- Reading a result: JUST TRUE is the text's yes; JUST FALSE is the text's no in its own words; NOTHING is "the text does not say"
-- (NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING (sge)"). A caller never turns NOTHING into FALSE.
--
-- Section 364 states no offence and no penalty: its only sanction is the Court's order in subsection (4). Nothing here invents one.

DECLARE `s 364 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 364(1) complete and have ready for delivery appropriate certificates in respect of all persons registered as holders of existing shares or debentures`
    `s 364(4) make good the default in complying with section 364`

§ `Section 364(1): the certificates`

-- "Within 60 days after the date of registration of the company, the company must complete and have ready for delivery appropriate certificates
-- in respect of all persons registered as holders of existing shares or debentures (as the case may be) as at the date of registration."
-- First, for whom: a person registered as a holder as at the date of registration. A person who was not so registered is outside the duty,
-- which names the holders and says nothing of anyone else (a scope limit with no "only": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, (c)).
-- src:23548 | 364.—(1) Within 60 days after the date of registration of the
-- src:23549 | company, the company must complete and have ready for delivery
-- src:23550 | appropriate certificates in respect of all persons registered as holders
-- src:23551 | of existing shares or debentures (as the case may be) as at the date of
-- src:23552 | registration.
@ref s 364(1) (src:23548-23552)
GIVEN `the person was registered as a holder of existing shares as at the date of registration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was registered as a holder of existing debentures as at the date of registration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 364(1) the company must complete and have ready for delivery appropriate certificates in respect of the person` MEANS
    IF `the person was registered as a holder of existing shares as at the date of registration` OR `the person was registered as a holder of existing debentures as at the date of registration`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in respect of all persons registered as holders of existing shares or debentures (as the case may be) as at the date of registration" names the persons it covers and says nothing of anyone else (the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, (c); fork line F-364-1 in NOTES.md)

-- The last day: 60 days after the date of registration of the company.
-- src:23548 | 364.—(1) Within 60 days after the date of registration of the
-- src:23549 | company, the company must complete and have ready for delivery
@ref s 364(1) (src:23548-23549)
GIVEN `the date of registration of the company` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 364(1) the last day for completing and having ready for delivery the certificates` MEANS
    `period: the last day of a period after` `the date of registration of the company` 60 Days

-- Whether the company has done it in time. JUST TRUE when the certificates were ready on or before the last day; JUST FALSE when they were
-- ready late, or are not ready and the 60 days have run out (a period the text fixes in its own words: the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, (a));
-- NOTHING while the 60 days still run and the certificates are not yet ready.
-- src:23548 | 364.—(1) Within 60 days after the date of registration of the
-- src:23549 | company, the company must complete and have ready for delivery
-- src:23550 | appropriate certificates in respect of all persons registered as holders
-- src:23551 | of existing shares or debentures (as the case may be) as at the date of
-- src:23552 | registration.
@ref s 364(1) (src:23548-23552)
GIVEN `the date of registration of the company` IS A DATE
      `the company has completed and has ready for delivery appropriate certificates in respect of all persons registered as holders of existing shares or debentures as at the date of registration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the certificates were completed and ready for delivery` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the question is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 364(1) the company has completed and has ready for delivery the certificates within 60 days after the date of registration` MEANS
    IF `the company has completed and has ready for delivery appropriate certificates in respect of all persons registered as holders of existing shares or debentures as at the date of registration`
    THEN (IF `period: the date is within a period after` `the date of registration of the company` `the date the certificates were completed and ready for delivery` 60 Days
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Within 60 days after the date of registration of the company, the company must complete and have ready ..." (ready, but after the 60 days: a period the text fixes in its own words, the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, (a))
    ELSE (IF `the date on which the question is asked` GREATER THAN `s 364(1) the last day for completing and having ready for delivery the certificates` `the date of registration of the company`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Within 60 days after the date of registration of the company": the 60 days have run out and the certificates are not ready
          ELSE NOTHING)     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the 60 days have not yet run out, so the duty is neither met nor missed

-- The duty as a regulative rule: 60 days from the date of registration (AT 0). The text's "the company must" names the company as the party.
-- src:23548 | 364.—(1) Within 60 days after the date of registration of the
-- src:23549 | company, the company must complete and have ready for delivery
-- src:23550 | appropriate certificates in respect of all persons registered as holders
-- src:23551 | of existing shares or debentures (as the case may be) as at the date of
-- src:23552 | registration.
@ref s 364(1) (src:23548-23552)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 364 act`
`s 364(1) the company must complete and have ready for delivery the certificates within 60 days after the date of registration` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 364(1) complete and have ready for delivery appropriate certificates in respect of all persons registered as holders of existing shares or debentures`
    WITHIN 60
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "appropriate certificates were not completed and ready for delivery within 60 days after the date of registration (section 364(1)); the holder may seek the Court's order under section 364(4)"

§ `Section 364(2): the prior certificates cease to be operative`

-- "Upon the delivery of the certificates to the holders of existing shares or debentures under subsection (1), all prior certificates in
-- respect of such shares or debentures cease to be operative and cease to have any validity for the purposes of this Act."
-- Two effects, each "Upon" the delivery: an "upon" counts as a "where" (the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, (b), and the ruling of the same day
-- that "when", "upon" and "whenever" count as "where"), so before delivery each is JUST FALSE. A certificate that is not "in respect of such
-- shares or debentures" is outside the subsection and the text says nothing of it.
-- src:23556 | (2) Upon the delivery of the certificates to the holders of existing
-- src:23557 | shares or debentures under subsection (1), all prior certificates in
-- src:23558 | respect of such shares or debentures cease to be operative and cease to
-- src:23559 | have any validity for the purposes of this Act.
@ref s 364(2) (src:23556-23559)
GIVEN `the prior certificate is in respect of shares or debentures whose new certificates have been delivered to their holders under section 364(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the new certificates have been delivered to the holders under section 364(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 364(2) the prior certificate has ceased to be operative` MEANS
    IF NOT `the prior certificate is in respect of shares or debentures whose new certificates have been delivered to their holders under section 364(1)`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "all prior certificates in respect of such shares or debentures": a certificate in respect of other shares or debentures is not named, and the text says nothing of it
    ELSE (IF `the new certificates have been delivered to the holders under section 364(1)`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Upon the delivery of the certificates ... all prior certificates ... cease to be operative" (not yet delivered: an "upon" read as "where", fork line F-364-2 in NOTES.md)

-- src:23556 | (2) Upon the delivery of the certificates to the holders of existing
-- src:23557 | shares or debentures under subsection (1), all prior certificates in
-- src:23558 | respect of such shares or debentures cease to be operative and cease to
-- src:23559 | have any validity for the purposes of this Act.
@ref s 364(2) (src:23556-23559)
GIVEN `the prior certificate is in respect of shares or debentures whose new certificates have been delivered to their holders under section 364(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the new certificates have been delivered to the holders under section 364(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 364(2) the prior certificate has ceased to have any validity for the purposes of this Act` MEANS
    IF NOT `the prior certificate is in respect of shares or debentures whose new certificates have been delivered to their holders under section 364(1)`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "all prior certificates in respect of such shares or debentures": a certificate in respect of other shares or debentures is not named, and the text says nothing of it
    ELSE (IF `the new certificates have been delivered to the holders under section 364(1)`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Upon the delivery of the certificates ... all prior certificates ... cease to have any validity for the purposes of this Act" (not yet delivered: an "upon" read as "where", fork line F-364-2 in NOTES.md)

§ `Section 364(3): bearer share warrants are void`

-- "Any share warrant, stating that the bearer of the warrant is entitled to the shares specified in the warrant and enabling the shares to be
-- transferred by delivery of the warrant, that had been issued by the foreign corporate entity before the date of registration of the company is void."
-- A flat statement that a class of warrant is void. For a document outside the class the text says nothing (a scope limit with no "only").
-- src:23563 | (3) Any share warrant, stating that the bearer of the warrant is
-- src:23564 | entitled to the shares specified in the warrant and enabling the shares
-- src:23565 | to be transferred by delivery of the warrant, that had been issued by
-- src:23566 | the foreign corporate entity before the date of registration of the
-- src:23567 | company is void.
@ref s 364(3) (src:23563-23567)
GIVEN `the document is a share warrant stating that the bearer of the warrant is entitled to the shares specified in the warrant and enabling the shares to be transferred by delivery of the warrant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the share warrant was issued by the foreign corporate entity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the share warrant was issued` IS A DATE
      `the date of registration of the company` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 364(3) the share warrant is void` MEANS
    IF `the document is a share warrant stating that the bearer of the warrant is entitled to the shares specified in the warrant and enabling the shares to be transferred by delivery of the warrant`
       AND `the share warrant was issued by the foreign corporate entity`
       AND `the date the share warrant was issued` LESS THAN `the date of registration of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection makes void "Any share warrant ... that had been issued by the foreign corporate entity before the date of registration of the company"; for any other document it says nothing about validity (the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, (c); fork line F-364-3 in NOTES.md)

§ `Section 364(4): the Court's order to make good the default`

-- "If any company on which a notice has been served requiring the company to make good any default in complying with this section fails to
-- make good the default within 10 days after the service of the notice, the Court may, on the application of the person entitled to have the
-- certificates or the debentures delivered to the person, make an order directing the company and any officer of the company to make good
-- the default within such time as is specified in the order".
-- The company's failure first: it made good the default within the 10 days after service, or it did not. JUST TRUE when it failed (made good
-- late, or has not made good and the 10 days have run out); JUST FALSE when it made good in time; NOTHING while the 10 days still run and
-- nothing is made good (neither failed nor succeeded yet). The text does not say who serves the notice: a plain input.
-- src:23571 | (4) If any company on which a notice has been served requiring the
-- src:23572 | company to make good any default in complying with this section
-- src:23573 | fails to make good the default within 10 days after the service of the
@ref s 364(4) (src:23571-23573)
GIVEN `a notice has been served on the company requiring the company to make good a default in complying with section 364` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the notice was served` IS A DATE
      `the company has made good the default` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the company made good the default` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the question is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 364(4) the company has failed to make good the default within 10 days after the service of the notice` MEANS
    IF NOT `a notice has been served on the company requiring the company to make good a default in complying with section 364`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If any company on which a notice has been served requiring the company to make good any default ... fails to make good the default within 10 days": no such notice, no such failure (a "where" gate: the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, (b))
    ELSE (IF `the company has made good the default`
          THEN (IF `period: the date is within a period after` `the date the notice was served` `the date the company made good the default` 10 Days
                THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the default was made good "within 10 days after the service of the notice", so there is no failure
                ELSE JUST TRUE)
          ELSE (IF `the date on which the question is asked` GREATER THAN `period: the last day of a period after` `the date the notice was served` 10 Days
                THEN JUST TRUE
                ELSE NOTHING))   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the 10 days after service have not yet run out and the default is not yet made good, so the company has neither failed nor succeeded

-- Then the Court's power: "the Court may, on the application of the person entitled to have the certificates or the debentures delivered to the
-- person, make an order". Two gates on a "may", each JUST FALSE when it fails: the failure ("If ... fails to make good", a "where" gate) and
-- the application ("on the application of", read as "upon": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, (b) and (c); fork line F-364-4 in NOTES.md).
-- src:23571 | (4) If any company on which a notice has been served requiring the
-- src:23572 | company to make good any default in complying with this section
-- src:23573 | fails to make good the default within 10 days after the service of the
-- src:23574 | notice, the Court may, on the application of the person entitled to have
-- src:23579 | the certificates or the debentures delivered to the person, make an
-- src:23580 | order directing the company and any officer of the company to make
-- src:23581 | good the default within such time as is specified in the order, and the
@ref s 364(4) (src:23571-23581)
GIVEN `the company has failed to make good the default within 10 days after the service of the notice, as section 364(4) reads` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application to the Court is made by the person entitled to have the certificates or the debentures delivered to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 364(4) the Court may make an order directing the company and any officer of the company to make good the default` MEANS
    IF NOT `the company has failed to make good the default within 10 days after the service of the notice, as section 364(4) reads`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If any company ... fails to make good the default within 10 days after the service of the notice, the Court may" (the "If" is not met: a "where" gate, the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, (b))
    ELSE (IF `the application to the Court is made by the person entitled to have the certificates or the debentures delivered to the person`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the Court may, on the application of the person entitled to have the certificates or the debentures delivered to the person, make an order" (an "on application" gate read as "upon": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, (b) and (c))

-- Who the order may direct: "the company and any officer of the company". A grant naming its persons; for anyone else, nothing is granted
-- and nothing said (the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1; fork line F-364-5 in NOTES.md).
DECLARE `s 364(4) person` IS ONE OF
    `s 364(4) the company`
    `s 364(4) an officer of the company who is in default`
    `s 364(4) an officer of the company who is not in default`
    `s 364(4) another person`

-- src:23579 | the certificates or the debentures delivered to the person, make an
-- src:23580 | order directing the company and any officer of the company to make
-- src:23581 | good the default within such time as is specified in the order, and the
@ref s 364(4) (src:23579-23581)
GIVEN `the person` IS A `s 364(4) person`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 364(4) the order may direct the person to make good the default` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the person`
    WHEN `s 364(4) the company` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 364(4) an officer of the company who is in default` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 364(4) an officer of the company who is not in default` THEN JUST TRUE   -- "any officer of the company": the direction is not limited to an officer in default
    WHEN `s 364(4) another person` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "directing the company and any officer of the company" names its persons and says nothing of anyone else

-- Costs: "the order may provide that all costs of and incidental to the application are to be borne by the company or by any officer of the company
-- in default in such proportions as the Court thinks fit". Read as: the company, or an officer in default. An officer not in default is not named.
-- src:23581 | good the default within such time as is specified in the order, and the
-- src:23582 | order may provide that all costs of and incidental to the application
-- src:23583 | are to be borne by the company or by any officer of the company in
-- src:23584 | default in such proportions as the Court thinks fit.
@ref s 364(4) (src:23581-23584)
GIVEN `the person` IS A `s 364(4) person`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 364(4) the order may provide that the costs of and incidental to the application are to be borne by the person` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the person`
    WHEN `s 364(4) the company` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 364(4) an officer of the company who is in default` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 364(4) an officer of the company who is not in default` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "borne by the company or by any officer of the company in default": "in default" is read as qualifying the officer; the other reading (it qualifies the company and the officer alike) is for a lawyer (fork line F-364-6 in NOTES.md)
    WHEN `s 364(4) another person` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the costs are laid on the company or an officer in default, and the text says nothing of anyone else

-- "in such proportions as the Court thinks fit" and "within such time as is specified in the order" are the Court's judgments: the time is an input to
-- the rules below, the proportions are not modelled (nothing in the text constrains them).

-- The order's direction as a regulative rule: once an order specifies a time, the company (and each officer) must make good the default within it.
-- src:23579 | the certificates or the debentures delivered to the person, make an
-- src:23580 | order directing the company and any officer of the company to make
-- src:23581 | good the default within such time as is specified in the order, and the
@ref s 364(4) (src:23579-23581)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
      `the number of days the order specifies for making good the default` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 364 act`
`s 364(4) the company must make good the default within the time the order specifies` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 364(4) make good the default in complying with section 364`
    WITHIN `the number of days the order specifies for making good the default`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the default in complying with section 364 was not made good within the time specified in the Court's order"

-- src:23579 | the certificates or the debentures delivered to the person, make an
-- src:23580 | order directing the company and any officer of the company to make
-- src:23581 | good the default within such time as is specified in the order, and the
@ref s 364(4) (src:23579-23581)
GIVEN `the name of the officer` IS A STRING
      `the number of days the order specifies for making good the default` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 364 act`
`s 364(4) the officer must make good the default within the time the order specifies` MEANS
    PARTY Officer `the name of the officer`
    MUST `s 364(4) make good the default in complying with section 364`
    WITHIN `the number of days the order specifies for making good the default`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Officer `the name of the officer` BECAUSE "the default in complying with section 364 was not made good within the time specified in the Court's order"
